Relevant columns & their potential use  
- "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  
  • "repo_name": to join every repository with its files and contents  
  • "language" : to filter‑out any repo whose language list/value contains the substring “python” (case–insensitive)  

- "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"  
  • "repo_name": for joining to LANGUAGES and SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  • "path": to find files whose names include “readme.md” (case‑insensitive)  
  • "id": blob‑id that lets us fetch the actual text from SAMPLE_CONTENTS  

- "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS"  
  • "id": to join back to SAMPLE_FILES  
  • "content": to test whether the file text contains the phrase “Copyright (c)”  
  • "sample_repo_name": redundant for the final answer, but handy for quick checks  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
•  language ILIKE '%python%'  (reject those repos)  
•  path ILIKE '%readme.md%'   (keep only README files)  
•  content ILIKE '%copyright (c)%'  (check the phrase – the “(c)” is usually lower‑case c)  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (LIMIT 20) that gradually build toward the final analysis.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double‑quotes and the database / schema / table names match the catalog you supplied.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at how language values are stored
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Find a few repos whose language field clearly contains "python"
SELECT DISTINCT
  "repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE LOWER("language"::STRING) LIKE '%python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. List some repos whose language list/value does NOT mention "python"
SELECT DISTINCT
  "repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE LOWER("language"::STRING) NOT LIKE '%python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect file paths that look like a README (any extension) in a handful of repos
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE LOWER("path") LIKE '%readme.%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Restrict to README files whose names specifically end with 'readme.md'
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "path",
  "id"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"
WHERE LOWER("path") LIKE '%readme.md%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Join README files with their text blobs, show the first few characters
SELECT
  f."repo_name",
  f."path",
  LEFT(c."content", 120) AS "sample_text"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"  f
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
  ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE LOWER(f."path") LIKE '%readme.md%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Check for the phrase "Copyright (c)" inside any README file, regardless of repo language
SELECT
  f."repo_name",
  f."path"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"  f
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
  ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE LOWER(f."path") LIKE '%readme.md%'
  AND LOWER(c."content") LIKE '%copyright (c)%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Bring in language info so we can later filter out the python repos
SELECT
  l."repo_name",
  l."language",
  f."path",
  c."content"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"    f
  ON f."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
  ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE LOWER(f."path") LIKE '%readme.md%'
  AND LOWER(c."content") LIKE '%copyright (c)%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Count README files with & without the copyright phrase among NON‑python repos
SELECT
  SUM(CASE WHEN LOWER(c."content") LIKE '%copyright (c)%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "with_phrase",
  COUNT(*)                                                   AS "total_readmes"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"    f
  ON f."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
  ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE LOWER(l."language"::STRING) NOT LIKE '%python%'
  AND LOWER(f."path") LIKE '%readme.md%';
```

```sql
-- 10. Compute the proportion of README.md files that contain the phrase, for NON‑python repos
SELECT
  ROUND(
    100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN LOWER(c."content") LIKE '%copyright (c)%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) 
          / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 2
  ) AS "proportion_percent"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"       l
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES"    f
  ON f."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_CONTENTS" c
  ON c."id" = f."id"
WHERE LOWER(l."language"::STRING) NOT LIKE '%python%'
  AND LOWER(f."path") LIKE '%readme.md%';
```

These queries move from basic inspection toward the final computation of the requested proportion, all while staying within the available catalog and enclosing every identifier in the required double quotes.
